/** @page dev-layout Directory layout

## General

The source code tree is organized as follows:

@verbatim
    .amend/                                     "Amend" source code tool (see https://github.com/fromsawa/amend)
    cmake/                                      CMake related files and tools
    docs/                                       Documentation and its configuration 
    examples/                                   Examples directory
        {library}/                              - per {library} examples
        playground/                             - "unrelated" playground for development
                                                  Scratch space for experimental code and future testing. 
                                                  No documentation required — just quick (or not‑so‑quick) 
                                                  validation of ideas. Developers are encouraged to leave 
                                                  traces of their thinking process in the Git history.
    icons/                                      VidRe icons
    share/                                      Non-binary data (e.g. scripts)
        lua/                                    - Lua scripting.
    src/                                        Source code
        apps/                                   Applications folder
        libs/                                   Framework libraries
            {library}                           - _a_ framework library (e.g. "core", "device", etc.)
                CMakeLists.txt
                vidre/                          - headers and sources are kept in a single place
                    {library}/                  - library specific header folder
                        config.hh               - basic library configuration file
                        config.cc               (*)
                        ...                     - library specific source files and folders 
                    ...                         - additional source files or folders (**)
        lua                                     Lua libraries
        plugins                                 Plugin tree (***)
        vidre                                   Fundamental configuration
    tests                                       Unit test and benchmarks
        benchmark                               - benchmark tests
                                                  As with the 'examples/playground' folder above, the 
                                                  programs contained within here are for testing ideas.
        {library}                               - per-library unit tests
@endverbatim

<sup>*</sup> 
For development purposes, it is recommended to create an accompanying 
source file (even if otherwise empty) for every header. This allows to detect 
compilation errors early.

<sup>**</sup>
The "core" library provides a set of functionality distributed over several
directories. All other libraries should retain the "vidre/{library}" folder,
unless reasoning dictates otherwise.

<sup>***</sup>
The plugin directories may contain additional libraries that are not directly
part of the fundamental framework. These libraries are only built if conditions
for the succesful build are met.

*/
